---
#907: a context that `uses` a commons sum type never sees that type's
variant constructors as values — the emitter's per-context rebrand
re-exports the public name as a type alias only (ADR 0256). Constructing a
variant directly here must be rejected at `check` time, not left to surface
as a `tsc` failure on the emitted output. Covers both a free `fn` body and a
service handler body — the two independent paths the checker runs.
---
context app.main

uses geo.shapes

fn unitCircle() -> Shape {
  Circle(1.0)
}

service shapes {
  on call() -> Effect[Shape] {
    Effect.pure(Square(2.0))
  }
}
